{
  "decision": "map_front",
  "next_plan": null,
  "rationale": "Round 3 gained only +1.5% HV (1.86e+04) and we have exactly one round / 100 evals left, so the marginal value is in covering the unused part of the objective ranges rather than chasing local refinement. The feasible front lives entirely in pipelined and pipelined_m (pipelined_m dominant: 160 unique feasible, best luts_plus_ffs=1200; pipelined best feasible luts_plus_ffs=1860), and it is truncated on the area axis: it spans luts_plus_ffs 1200..3646 against the HV reference of 4000 (nothing below 1200 explored), while on the accuracy axis it over-covers (12.6..22.5 vs ref 12). Accuracy is therefore not the binding dimension; the unexplored cheap side (data_width 17..26 on the front, registry allows 8) is where remaining hypervolume and the min-luts_plus_ffs selection rule both point. All three constraints are comfortably reachable (throughput best 273 vs 32; max_abs_err best 5.36e-08 vs 2.44e-04; sys_p99_batch_us best 0.154 vs 0.44), so this is not infeasible. iterative is deliberately not added: it yields one result per N+3 cycles (and unrolled_k already produced 0 feasible with max throughput 10.3 MSPS), so it cannot clear the >=32 MSPS constraint and would waste budget. Spending the final round on a seeded NSGA-II over the full ranges of pipelined/pipelined_m maps the whole front, pushes into the <1200 LUT+FF region, and gives the L2 system re-selection the widest set of pass-margin candidates."
}

{

  "decision": "stop",

  "next_plan": null

,

  "rationale": "Budget and round cap are both exhausted (400/400 evals, round 4 of 4), so no further exploration is possible. The front is clearly feasible, not infeasible: every constraint has designs that pass with margin — throughput best seen 273 MSPS vs the >=32 requirement, max_abs_err best 5.36e-08 (2^-24.15) vs the 2^-12=2.44e-4 limit, and sys_p99_batch best 0.154 us vs the 0.44 us bound. The feasible front holds 22 designs (212 unique of 400 evals) and has good spread on both objectives: luts_plus_ffs 1200..3646 against the HV reference 4000, accuracy_bits 12.6..22.5 against the HV reference 12, giving HV 1.914e4 with a +2.9% gain in the last round. The selection rule (min luts_plus_ffs) is served directly by the front's cheapest point, pipelined_m [data_width=19 n_iter=14 angle_guard=2 frac_guard=0 rounding=trunc m=4] at luts_plus_ffs=1200, accuracy_bits=12.6 (max_abs_err 1.63e-4, still within the 2^-12 limit), 93.6 MSPS — comfortably meeting both the throughput and error constraints, with ample sys_p99_batch headroom relative to the 0.44 us bound for the L2 simulation. Since constraints are met, the curve is well covered, and no further evaluations remain, stop is the correct call."

